  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3786",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Kcnq3, as evidenced by multiple paths in the hetionet dataset, all of which score highly (final_score=0.6742). This binding is consistent across three distinct targets—Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnv2—each of which is associated with the same biological process: Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is directly linked to Kcnq3, suggesting a potential role for Guanidine in modulating potassium channel function. The shared involvement of these targets in the same biological process implies that Guanidine may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by influencing the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels, which are critical for maintaining cellular electrical stability. The high scores in the dataset suggest that the relationship is well-supported by the available evidence, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the functional significance of this interaction.",
